     1	/**
     2	 * Scoped to this molecule's own contract per testing.md: which of its two rows render, in which
     3	 * order, and whether the block itself renders at all.
     4	 *
     5	 * `app/utils/richText` is mocked, the same way the two child atoms' own suites mock it — its
     6	 * behaviour is exhaustively proven in app/utils/richText.test.tsx. The mocks are
     7	 * `mockImplementation`, not `mockReturnValue`: a fixed return ignores its argument, so a
     8	 * molecule that dropped `modelInfo` on the way to the atom, or handed the guard `styleCode`
     9	 * instead of `modelInfo`, would still produce exactly the render the test expected. Keying each
    10	 * mock off its input is what makes those two prop-to-state mistakes fail here.
    11	 *
    12	 * Renders go through `renderWithIntl` rather than a bare `render` — see that helper.
    13	 *
    14	 * The atoms are left real because composition is part of the contract: `index.tsx` fixes the
    15	 * model line above the style code, asserted below by position rather than by presence, and each
    16	 * atom must still collapse independently inside this wrapper.
    17	 *
    18	 * The all-absent case is the reason this file exists. This molecule's recipe carries a
    19	 * `paddingTop`, and padding is unconditional — unlike the `gap` that every other group in
    20	 * ui-kits/ relies on, it does not collapse when the children render nothing. Without the guard
    21	 * in index.tsx, a product with neither model copy nor a style code would push 28px of empty
    22	 * space below the accordions.
